## Risks / notes
- All new `ask`-level logic (caller-override suppression, read-back correction, density guard) is gated on `composesNew` and on `opts.brief`/premise presence; `verify-language` drives everything through `interpret` or through `ask` with only a `token` in `brief`, so those paths are untouched and the "used for" invariant still sees the unmodified parsed reading.
- The reference read-back is now **parsed** (`read.understood`, unchanged by ask) vs **outcome** (the corrected line + `applied`/`skipped`); a trait appears in `skipped` only when it was dropped, never simultaneously in `applied`.
- Caller-band suppression drops *all* tempo ops (mood, reference pull, and spoken absolute) when `opts.brief` pins a band — the spoken absolute yields to the programmatic caller by design, per the review.
- `_opDim` grouping only changes behaviour for mood+title combinations (empty `userDims` otherwise), which no existing test exercises; the partial-provenance path (`as hints`) likewise only triggers there.
- I could not run the suite; correctness rests on the reads above. The one place to watch is `'a calm song'` composing at exactly 150 — it relies on a maj-capable style whose band contains 150 (anthem/trance/arcade/punk all qualify), so `pickStyle` never empties and `bpm` rounds to 150.
